\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Lab topology used in this chapter and in chapter 6 for the evaluation. A single host runs every container --- the attacker (Kali with MITRE Caldera \cite {caldera2024}), the two victims with Wazuh agents and \texttt  {auditd}, the backing stores (PostgreSQL, Redis) and the user-facing surfaces (API, web, mobile). All containers share the \texttt  {172.18.0.0/16} bridge so the attacker can reach the victims directly.}}{44}{figure.5.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ch5:topology}{{5.2}{44}{Lab topology used in this chapter and in chapter 6 for the evaluation. A single host runs every container --- the attacker (Kali with MITRE Caldera \protect \cite {caldera2024}), the two victims with Wazuh agents and \texttt {auditd}, the backing stores (PostgreSQL, Redis) and the user-facing surfaces (API, web, mobile). All containers share the \texttt {172.18.0.0/16} bridge so the attacker can reach the victims directly}{figure.5.2}{}}
