\newlabel{fig:ch5:dqngating}{{5.22}{65}{The gating logic that wraps every DQN action. An intervention (\texttt {ESCALATE}, \texttt {ISOLATE\_HOST}, \texttt {BLOCK\_USER\_IP}) is only authorised when all four deterministic checks --- AE score, $\beta $-VAE probability, Transformer confidence and GNN node risk --- exceed their thresholds. Any single failure down-grades the action to \texttt {LOW\_ALERT}}{figure.5.22}{}}
